{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' .receipts-category-progress.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Receipts Category Harness Progress\n\n## Harness boundary\n\nMechanism: a Codex task-scoped specialist prompt documented in `.codex-receipts-category-specialist.md`, plus this persistent notes file at the fixture root.\n\nWhat it is meant to do: keep the work organized around one specialist responsibility: implement the Module 03 `--by-category` receipts task, touch only `receipts/` for product code, use only `tests/test_by_category.py` for verification, and write state here so a later invocation can resume cold.\n\nWhat it does not enforce: this is unenforced custom-instructions-scoped prompt text. Codex in this environment does not provide path-level sandboxing for `receipts/` only. The filesystem sandbox allows writes in this scratch fixture generally, so the boundary depends on following and verifying the declared scope. Network access is not needed and was not used.\n\nAllowed fixture-root exceptions: this notes file and the specialist definition are harness artifacts required by the exercise. The user also requested a README translation-table entry that states the Codex boundary limitation plainly.\n\n## Chronological state\n\n- Read Module 03 `AGENT.md`, `module.yaml`, and README up to but not including `Takeaway`.\n- Parsed the gate: bounded specialist, persistent state, actual run transcript/evidence, and reset/resume evidence.\n- Inspected fixture files: `receipts/grouping.py`, `receipts/cli.py`, `tests/test_by_category.py`, `tests/test_grouping.py`, `SPEC.md`, and `data/sample_receipts.csv`.\n- The scratch fixture is not a git repository, so `git status` cannot be used for isolation evidence here. Use explicit file listing and focused diffs/content checks instead.\n\n## Implementation reasoning\n\n- `group_expenses_by_category` should mirror the existing month grouping shape: parse row